.TH MDT.ENABLE_PARALLEL_RENAME_FILE 4 2026-10-06 Lustre "Lustre Kernel Interfaces"
.SH NAME
mdt.enable_parallel_rename_file \- parallel rename of files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY
.RI "lctl get_param mdt." FSNAME *.enable_parallel_rename_file
.SY
.RI "lctl set_param mdt." FSNAME *.enable_parallel_rename_file= ENABLE
.YS
.SS PROPERTIES
.TP
.B Access Permissions
.BR 644 | -rw-r--r--
.TP
.B Scope
.br
Per-MDT device.
.TP
.B Config
.br
Always present for MDT devices.
.TP
.B Default
.RB enable_parallel_rename_file= 1
.SH DESCRIPTION
The boolean
.B enable_parallel_rename_file
parameter controls whether renaming a non-directory may proceed without
the filesystem-wide rename lock, holding only the locks on the parent
directories and on the names involved.
If
.I ENABLE
is
.B 1
(or aliases
.BR on " or " true ),
a same-directory rename of a non-directory runs in parallel with other
renames. If it is
.B 0
or
.B off
every rename of a non-directory takes the rename lock.
.PP
A non-directory renamed between two directories is also governed by
.BR enable_parallel_rename_crossdir ,
and one whose source parent or source object is on another MDT by
.BR enable_parallel_rename_remote .
It takes the rename lock unless every one of them that applies permits
it. Directory renames are governed by
.BR enable_parallel_rename_dir .
.SH MODULES
This parameter is in the following module:
.EX
.B mdt.*.enable_parallel_rename_file
.EE
.SH EXAMPLES
Disable parallel rename of files on the
.B testfs
filesystem:
.EX
.RB "mgs# " "lctl set_param -P mdt.testfs-*.enable_parallel_rename_file=0"
.EE
.SH AVAILABILITY
The
.B enable_parallel_rename_file
parameter is part of the
.BR lustre (7)
filesystem package since release 2.16.0.
.\" Added in commit v2_15_50-213-gf238540c87
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mdt.enable_parallel_rename_crossdir (4),
.BR mdt.enable_parallel_rename_dir (4),
.BR mdt.enable_parallel_rename_remote (4),
.BR mdt.rename_stats (4),
.BR lustre (7),
.BR lctl-set_param (8)
